    "meta.projectAdventureTitle": "Adventure game — PyBot",
    "meta.projectAdventureDescription": "Build a choose-your-path text adventure in Python with rooms, choices, a loop and an inventory list.",
    "topic.progressProjectAdventure": "ZONE 12 · 4 OF 6",
    "projectAdventure.pybotNamed": "{name}, left or right? Every choice opens a new room!",
    "projectAdventure.eyebrow": "GAME PROJECTS · ADVENTURE",
    "projectAdventure.title": "Choose your own path.",
    "projectAdventure.intro": "Build a text adventure: rooms, choices, a bag of things, and a hidden treasure.",
    "projectAdventure.pybot": "Left or right? Every choice opens a new room!",
    "projectAdventure.robotLabel": "PyBot looks around with curiosity next to a gold trophy",
    "projectAdventure.life1Title": "Choose-your-path books",
    "projectAdventure.life1Text": "\"Open the door? Go to page 12. Run away? Go to page 30.\"",
    "projectAdventure.life2Title": "Adventure video games",
    "projectAdventure.life2Text": "You walk room to room, pick up keys, and open locked doors.",
    "projectAdventure.life3Title": "A treasure hunt",
    "projectAdventure.life3Text": "At a party, each clue sends you to a new place until you find the prize.",
    "projectAdventure.lifeTitle": "Stories where you choose.",
    "projectAdventure.lifeIntro": "You pick the path, and the story changes.",
    "projectAdventure.plan1Title": "Rooms",
    "projectAdventure.plan1Text": "A box keeps the room you are in. if and elif pick what happens there.",
    "projectAdventure.plan2Title": "Choices",
    "projectAdventure.plan2Text": "input() asks left, right or quit. An if inside another if makes a nested choice.",
    "projectAdventure.plan3Title": "The bag",
    "projectAdventure.plan3Text": "A list keeps what you find. append adds, and in checks.",
    "projectAdventure.plan4Title": "Keep playing",
    "projectAdventure.plan4Text": "A while loop repeats until you find the treasure or quit.",
    "projectAdventure.planEyebrow": "THE PLAN",
    "projectAdventure.planTitle": "Four small steps.",
    "projectAdventure.planIntro": "Each step uses something you already learned.",
    "projectAdventure.runCode": "inventory = []\nroom = \"hall\"\n\nwhile room != \"treasure\" and room != \"quit\":\n    if room == \"hall\":\n        choice = input(\"Hall: left, right or quit? \")\n        if choice == \"left\":\n            room = \"library\"\n        elif choice == \"right\":\n            room = \"kitchen\"\n        elif choice == \"quit\":\n            room = \"quit\"\n        else:\n            print(\"Only left, right or quit.\")\n    elif room == \"library\":\n        print(\"You find a key!\")\n        inventory.append(\"key\")\n        room = \"hall\"\n    elif room == \"kitchen\":\n        if \"key\" in inventory:\n            print(\"The key opens the chest.\")\n            room = \"treasure\"\n        else:\n            print(\"The chest is locked.\")\n            room = \"hall\"\n\nif room == \"treasure\":\n    print(\"You found the treasure!\")\nprint(\"Bag:\", inventory)",
    "projectAdventure.runAnswers": "right\nleft\nright",
    "thinking.adventure-predictSuccess": "Yes! The library put the key in the bag, so the kitchen opens. The last line shows the bag.",
    "thinking.adventure-predictHint": "Not yet. Follow the answers: right, then left, then right. Which room adds the key? What is printed last?",
    "projectAdventure.predictOpt1": "Bag: []",
    "projectAdventure.predictOpt2": "Bag: ['key']",
    "projectAdventure.predictOpt3": "The chest is locked.",
    "projectAdventure.runTitle": "Find the treasure.",
    "projectAdventure.predictScene": "Read the game in the editor. Then look at PyBot's answers.",
    "projectAdventure.predictAnswer": "PyBot's answers: right, left, right",
    "projectAdventure.predictQuestion": "What is the last line Python shows?",
    "projectAdventure.tryText": "Change PyBot's answers to: right, quit. Does the treasure line appear?",
    "projectAdventure.fixTunnelTitle": "Step 1: a choice inside a choice",
    "projectAdventure.fixTunnelTask": "In the tunnel, PyBot asks about the torch but does nothing with it. Add the if and else.",
    "projectAdventure.fixTunnelCode": "choice = input(\"Door or tunnel? \")\nif choice == \"door\":\n    print(\"The door is locked.\")\nelif choice == \"tunnel\":\n    torch = input(\"Light the torch? yes or no? \")\n    # Add an if inside: yes prints \"You see gold!\"\n    # Add an else: it prints \"It is too dark.\"\n",
    "projectAdventure.fixTunnelExpected": "Door or tunnel? tunnel\nLight the torch? yes or no? yes\nYou see gold!",
    "thinking.adventure-tunnelSuccess": "Great! The if is inside the elif, so the torch question only matters in the tunnel.",
    "thinking.adventure-tunnelHint": "Not yet. Under torch = input(...), write if torch == \"yes\": with more spaces in front, then an else.",
    "projectAdventure.fixTunnelAnswers": "tunnel\nyes",
    "projectAdventure.fixBagTitle": "Step 2: the bag",
    "projectAdventure.fixBagTask": "PyBot finds a torch but forgets to keep it. Put it in the bag.",
    "projectAdventure.fixBagCode": "bag = []\nprint(\"You find a torch!\")\n# Put \"torch\" in the bag with append.\n\nif \"torch\" in bag:\n    print(\"The cave lights up.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"It is too dark to walk.\")\nprint(\"Bag:\", bag)\n",
    "projectAdventure.fixBagExpected": "You find a torch!\nThe cave lights up.\nBag: ['torch']",
    "thinking.adventure-bagSuccess": "Yes! append put the torch in the list, so in finds it.",
    "thinking.adventure-bagHint": "Not yet. Replace the comment with bag.append(\"torch\").",
