    "projectEightBall.predictQuestion": "How many times does Python show \"The ball says:\"?",
    "projectEightBall.tryText": "Run it twice. The answers may change, but the number of answers stays the same.",
    "projectEightBall.fixAddTitle": "Step 1: more answers",
    "projectEightBall.fixAddTask": "The ball only has two answers. Add \"Maybe.\" to the list.",
    "projectEightBall.fixAddCode": "import random\n\nanswers = [\"Yes!\", \"No way.\"]\n# Add \"Maybe.\" to the list with append.\n\nprint(answers)\nprint(random.choice(answers) in answers)\n",
    "projectEightBall.fixAddExpected": "['Yes!', 'No way.', 'Maybe.']\nTrue",
    "thinking.ball-addSuccess": "Yes! append adds the answer at the end. Whatever random.choice picks, it is in the list, so True.",
    "thinking.ball-addHint": "Not yet. Replace the comment with answers.append(\"Maybe.\").",
    "projectEightBall.fixReturnTitle": "Step 2: give the answer back",
    "projectEightBall.fixReturnTask": "shake() picks an answer but never gives it back, so reply is None. Fix the function.",
    "projectEightBall.fixReturnCode": "import random\n\nanswers = [\"Yes!\", \"No way.\", \"Maybe.\"]\n\ndef shake():\n    random.choice(answers)\n\nreply = shake()\nprint(reply in answers)\n",
    "projectEightBall.fixReturnExpected": "True",
    "thinking.ball-returnSuccess": "Fixed! return gives the picked answer back, and it is always one from the list.",
    "thinking.ball-returnHint": "Not yet. Write return before random.choice inside the function.",
    "projectEightBall.fixLoopTitle": "Step 3: keep asking",
    "projectEightBall.fixLoopTask": "PyBot fixed the answer to test the loop. It should answer until bye, but it stops at once. Fix the while.",
    "projectEightBall.fixLoopCode": "def shake():\n    return \"Maybe.\"  # fixed answer, only for testing\n\nquestion = input(\"Your question: \")\nwhile question == \"bye\":\n    print(\"The ball says:\", shake())\n    question = input(\"Your question: \")\nprint(\"Bye!\")\n",
    "projectEightBall.fixLoopExpected": "Your question: Will I fly?\nThe ball says: Maybe.\nYour question: bye\nBye!",
