    "meta.turtleArtTitle": "Art with functions — PyBot",
    "meta.turtleArtDescription": "Draw a scene with turtle functions: a filled square, a roof, a sun, and trees, placed with goto and painted with begin_fill and end_fill.",
    "topic.progressTurtleArt": "ZONE 13 · 3 OF 3",
    "turtleArt.pybotNamed": "{name}, I made a house function. Now we can build a whole street!",
    "turtleArt.robotLabel": "PyBot stands proud next to a little turtle that leaves a dashed line as it walks",
    "turtleArt.pybot": "I made a house function. Now I can build a whole street!",
    "turtleArt.eyebrow": "TURTLE DRAWING · ART",
    "turtleArt.title": "Functions paint a picture.",
    "turtleArt.intro": "Put each drawing in a function. Then call them to build a house, a sun and trees.",
    "turtleArt.life1Title": "A cookie cutter",
    "turtleArt.life1Text": "One cutter, many cookies. Each cookie can get a different icing.",
    "turtleArt.life2Title": "Building blocks",
    "turtleArt.life2Text": "Build a wall piece and a roof piece, then snap them into a house.",
    "turtleArt.life3Title": "Coloring a page",
    "turtleArt.life3Text": "First draw the outline, then fill the inside with color.",
    "turtleArt.lifeTitle": "Make it once, use it often.",
    "turtleArt.lifeIntro": "Artists and builders reuse pieces all the time.",
    "turtleArt.look1Title": "A function draws",
    "turtleArt.look1Text": "def square(size, fill) keeps the steps. square(50, \"red\") draws one.",
    "turtleArt.look2Title": "Fill it in",
    "turtleArt.look2Text": "color(\"black\", \"yellow\"): black pen, yellow inside. begin_fill() and end_fill() wrap the shape.",
    "turtleArt.look3Title": "Jump with goto",
    "turtleArt.look3Text": "penup(), goto(x, y), pendown() moves the turtle to a new spot without a line.",
    "turtleArt.lookTitle": "Three tools for art.",
    "turtleArt.walk1": "def square(size, fill):",
    "turtleArt.walk1Tag": "A function with two parameters: how big, and which paint.",
    "turtleArt.walk2": "    t.color(\"black\", fill)",
    "turtleArt.walk2Tag": "Black pen. The inside gets the color in fill.",
    "turtleArt.walk3": "    t.begin_fill()",
    "turtleArt.walk3Tag": "Starts the shape that will get painted.",
    "turtleArt.walk4": "    for i in range(4):",
    "turtleArt.walk4Tag": "The square loop from the last page.",
    "turtleArt.walk5": "        t.forward(size)",
    "turtleArt.walk5Tag": "Each side is as long as size.",
    "turtleArt.walk6": "        t.left(90)",
    "turtleArt.walk6Tag": "One corner.",
    "turtleArt.walk7": "    t.end_fill()",
    "turtleArt.walk7Tag": "Pours the paint inside the square.",
    "turtleArt.walk8": "def move(x, y):",
    "turtleArt.walk8Tag": "A helper to jump to any spot.",
    "turtleArt.walk9": "    t.penup()",
    "turtleArt.walk9Tag": "Lift the pen: no line while jumping.",
    "turtleArt.walk10": "    t.goto(x, y)",
    "turtleArt.walk10Tag": "Go to x (sideways) and y (up or down). The middle is (0, 0).",
    "turtleArt.walk11": "    t.pendown()",
    "turtleArt.walk11Tag": "Pen down, ready to draw.",
    "turtleArt.walk12": "move(-50, 20)",
    "turtleArt.walk12Tag": "Jumps to 50 left and 20 up.",
    "turtleArt.walk13": "square(60, \"pink\")",
    "turtleArt.walk13Tag": "Draws a pink square there.",
    "turtleArt.walkNoteTitle": "The screen:",
    "turtleArt.walkNoteText": "It is 400 steps wide and 400 tall. x goes from -200 to 200, and y too.",
    "turtleArt.walkTitle": "Read it line by line.",
    "turtleArt.walkIntro": "A painted square on the left, a jump on the right.",
    "turtleArt.runCode": "import turtle\nt = turtle.Turtle()\nturtle.bgcolor(\"lightblue\")\n\ndef move(x, y):\n    t.penup()\n    t.goto(x, y)\n    t.pendown()\n\ndef square(size, fill):\n    t.color(\"black\", fill)\n    t.begin_fill()\n    for i in range(4):\n        t.forward(size)\n        t.left(90)\n    t.end_fill()\n\ndef roof(size, fill):\n    t.color(\"black\", fill)\n    t.begin_fill()\n    for i in range(3):\n        t.forward(size)\n        t.left(120)\n    t.end_fill()\n\nmove(-150, -120)\nsquare(120, \"orange\")\nmove(-150, 0)\nroof(120, \"red\")\nmove(100, 50)\nt.color(\"orange\", \"gold\")\nt.begin_fill()\nt.circle(45)\nt.end_fill()",
    "thinking.art-predictSuccess": "Yes! square(120, \"orange\") paints the walls, roof(120, \"red\") the roof, and the last lines paint the sun.",
    "thinking.art-predictHint": "Not yet. Find each call and its colors. The functions draw when they are called.",
    "turtleArt.predictScene": "An orange house with a red roof, and a gold sun",
    "turtleArt.predictSun": "Only the sun: functions never draw",
    "turtleArt.predictSwap": "A red house with an orange roof",
    "turtleArt.runTitle": "PyBot paints a little scene.",
    "turtleArt.predictQuestion": "What will the turtle draw?",
    "turtleArt.tryText": "Add two lines at the end: move(-110, -120), then square(40, \"brown\") for a door.",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayScene": "A function keeps drawing steps so you can use them again.",
    "thinking.art-everydaySuccess": "Yes! You make the stamp once, then press it anywhere. A function is made once and called many times.",
    "thinking.art-everydayHint": "Not yet. Look for something you make once and then use many times.",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayStamp": "A rubber stamp you press again and again",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayEraser": "An eraser",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayPage": "A blank page",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayTitle": "Like a function in real life",
    "turtleArt.quizEverydayQuestion": "Which one works like a drawing function?",
    "turtleArt.quizDefCode": "def triangle():\n    for i in range(3):\n        t.forward(80)\n        t.left(120)",
    "thinking.art-defSuccess": "Right! def only keeps the steps. The turtle draws when a line calls triangle().",
    "thinking.art-defHint": "Not yet. def is like writing a recipe. Is anyone cooking it yet?",
    "turtleArt.quizDefTriangle": "A triangle",
    "turtleArt.quizDefNothing": "Nothing yet: no line calls the function",
    "turtleArt.quizDefError": "An error",
    "turtleArt.quizDefTitle": "Only the def",
